.TH AVR\-JOB\-VIEW 1 "" "avr 0.3.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-job-view \- View a single job with its steps.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr job view
[OPTIONS] JOB_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
View a single job with its steps.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr job view job-abc123
    avr job view job-abc123 --log-failed
    avr job view job-abc123 --json conclusion,steps
    avr job view job-abc123 --json '*' --jq '.steps[] | select(.conclusion=="failure")'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    completed_at, conclusion, created_at, duration_seconds, platform_job_id,
    platform_run_id, job_id, job_name, labels, repository, repository_id,
    running_on_avrea, started_at, state, steps, workflow_run
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIJOB_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR
Print full logs for the job.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-failed\fR
Print logs only for failed steps.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.TP
\fB\-\-web\fR
Open in browser.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print logs directly to stdout instead of paging through `less`. Same as setting AVR_PAGER=''.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-job (1),
.BR avr-job-list (1),
.BR avr-job-logs (1),
.BR avr-job-metrics (1),
.BR avr-job-ssh (1),
.BR avr-job-watch (1)
